{
    "about": "Shared cases of the seal of the content store (decision R104, documentation/Canonical Form.md, \"The seal of the content store\"). The TypeScript and the Rust implementation both read this file. A key is never stored as text: a case gives the byte that its key repeats (\"keyByte\", \"keyLength\" bytes, 32 when not given), and <key> in a text is the 64 small hexadecimal digits of that key, <KEY> the same in capital letters, built at run time. The HMAC cases are test cases 1 and 6 of RFC 4231. A difference case gives the files of the sealed commit and of the last commit, the texts of their files by \"<commit>:<path>\", the difference and its text.",
    "hmac": [
        {
            "name": "RFC 4231, test case 1",
            "keyByte": "0b",
            "keyLength": 20,
            "text": "Hi There",
            "hmac": "b0344c61d8db38535ca8afceaf0bf12b881dc200c9833da726e9376c2e32cff7"
        },
        {
            "name": "RFC 4231, test case 6: a key longer than a block",
            "keyByte": "aa",
            "keyLength": 131,
            "text": "Test Using Larger Than Block-Size Key - Hash Key First",
            "hmac": "60e431591ee0b67f0d8a26aacbf5b77f8e0bc6213728c5140546040f0ee37f54"
        }
    ],
    "env": [
